We have access to public methods: peek() returns head element (or null if empty?). In PriorityQueue, peek returns null if empty. size() returns size.

We need to refer to old head element: \old(this.peek())? But after removal, the method may modify the queue. So we can use \old(this.peek()) for old head before removal. After removal, we have this.peek().

