analysisWe need to write an assert statement for the comment at end of remove method.

Comment: "If the queue is not empty, the element at the head of the queue after removal is greater than or equal to the element that was at the head before removal."

Interpretation: After removing an element (any element), if the queue is not empty after removal, then the new head element (peek()) is >= old head element (peek before removal). In priority queue, head is least element. So after removal, head should be >= previous head (since smallest element might have been removed, new smallest is greater or equal). Need to capture condition: queue not empty after removal. Also need to refer to old head before removal: \old(this.peek()).

Thus assert: (!\old(this.isEmpty())? maybe need to check before removal? The comment says "If the queue is not empty, the element at the head of the queue after removal is greater than or equal to the element that was at the head before removal." That implies precondition: queue not empty before removal? Actually removal could be called on empty queue; then nothing changes. The statement says "If the queue is not empty, the element at the head of the queue after removal is greater than or equal to the element that was at the head before removal." So precondition: before removal, queue not empty. After removal, if resulting queue not empty, then new head >= old head. But if removal removed the head element, then new head will be >= old head (since old head removed). If removal removed some other element, head may stay same, which is >= old head (equal). So condition holds.

Thus assert: (!\old(this.isEmpty())) => (this.size()>0 => this.peek().compareTo(\old(this.peek())) >= 0). But we need to use public methods: peek() returns E, which must be comparable? The class may have comparator; we can use compareTo or comparator. However we cannot call compareTo directly in spec? Usually spec can use .compareTo. It's okay. Use ((Comparable<E>)this.peek()).compareTo(\old(this.peek())) >=0 if natural ordering. But there is also comparator() method. To be generic, we could say: if comparator != null then comparator.compare(this.peek(), \old(this.peek())) >=0 else ((Comparable<E>)this.peek()).compareTo(\old(this.peek())) >=0. But spec may be simpler: this.peek().compareTo(\old(this.peek())) >= 0 assuming natural ordering. However spec may need to use comparator if present. In examples they used methods like this.index_of, etc. Not using comparator.

Simplify: assert (!\old(this.isEmpty())) => (this.size() == 0 || this.peek().compareTo(\old(this.peek())) >= 0);

But we need method isEmpty? Not defined in class snippet but AbstractQueue provides isEmpty via size() ==0. Could use this.size()>0. Use this.size()>0 => ... . However we also need to consider old size maybe zero. So condition: \old(this.size()) > 0 => (this.size() == 0 || this.peek().compareTo(\old(this.peek())) >= 0). But comment says "If the queue is not empty, the element at the head of the queue after removal is greater than or equal to the element that was at the head before removal." It doesn't specify case where after removal empty; then condition vacuously true. So we can assert: \old(this.size()) > 0 => (this.size() == 0 || this.peek().compareTo(\old(this.peek())) >= 0).

